cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "torch_vn_algebra: finite-dimensional Type I von Neumann algebras in PyTorch"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Irina
    family-names: Nikolaeva
  - given-names: Andrej
    family-names: Novikov
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/andre-a-no/von_neumann_type_i"
keywords:
  - von Neumann algebra
  - operator algebra
  - quantum information
  - quantum channels
  - random matrices
  - superselection sectors
  - spin chains
  - PyTorch
  - GPU
abstract: >-
  Batched operators, states, channels and constrained optimisation in
  finite-dimensional Type I von Neumann algebras (direct sums of matrix
  algebras), with block-diagonal storage, exact Haar sampling, functional
  calculus with spectral gradients, channels between sectors, tensor
  products with charge fusion, spin chains with U(1) and momentum sectors,
  Krylov solvers and Lindblad dynamics, on CPUs and GPUs.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Finite-Dimensional Type I von Neumann Algebras in PyTorch: A GPU-Accelerated Framework for Random Block-Diagonal Operators"
  authors:
